{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/3/des.md && printf '\\\\n===== prompt =====\\\\n' && sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/3/prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将每个前景对象的像素按照其在对象内的局部坐标，映射到一个全局颜色查找表中获取新颜色，从而重绘整个对象。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格左上角有一个小的 NxN 彩色方阵作为颜色查找表，每个单元格为不同颜色（使用 Red、Blue、Green、Yellow、Grey 等）。\n  - 网格其他区域散布着若干个大小恰好为 NxN 的 4-连通单色矩形前景对象，每个对象使用同一种 Grey 颜色。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个 Grey 矩形对象，将其 NxN 内的每个像素按局部坐标 (r,c) 查找颜色表中 (r,c) 位置的颜色。\n  - 用查找到的颜色替换该像素的 Grey 色。\n  - 保留颜色查找表本身不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：Grey 对象看似相同，但它们的重着色结果由位置无关的全局查找表决定；查找表的空间结构映射到每个对象的内部坐标，这是一种自掩码（self-mask）机制的变体。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据每个封闭区域的开口方向，将该区域内部的散布标记像素沿开口方向\"倾倒\"出去，在区域外部排成一列。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Azure。\n  - 网格中有若干个由 Maroon 像素构成的 U 形或 C 形半封闭容器（一像素厚边框，三面封闭、一面开口）。\n  - 每个容器内部散布着若干个不同颜色的单像素标记（如 Red、Green、Yellow）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个容器，确定其开口方向（上、下、左、右）。\n  - 将容器内部的所有标记像素从开口处\"倾倒\"出去：沿开口方向逐个排列在容器外部的第一列/行背景像素上。\n  - 标记的排列顺序为：距离开口最近的标记排在最外面（即先倒出），距离最远的排在最里面（最后倒出）。\n  - 清除容器内部的标记像素为背景色。容器本体保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：开口方向决定倾倒方向，标记像素到开口的距离决定排列顺序；容器的形状本身提供了全部的空间指令。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：检测每个前景对象的对称类型（水平对称、垂直对称、旋转对称或无对称），按对称类型将对象移动到网格的指定区域。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格被 Grey 色的十字线（一条完整水平线和一条完整垂直线）分为四个象限。\n  - 网格中散布着若干个多色 4-连通前景对象，每个对象的形状属于以下四种对称类型之一：仅水平反射对称、仅垂直反射对称、180 度旋转对称（但非反射对称）、无对称性。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 水平反射对称的对象移动到左上象限。\n  - 垂直反射对称的对象移动到右上象限。\n  - 180 度旋转对称的对象移动到左下象限。\n  - 无对称性的对象移动到右下象限。\n  - 在目标象限中，对象保持原色和形状，紧贴象限角落放置。多个同类对象按原始行优先顺序依次排列，间隔一像素。\n  - 清除原始位置的对象。保持十字分隔线不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：对称类型是分类标签而非变换操作；十字线不是对称轴，而是输出区域的分隔符；解题者需要对每个对象独立分析对称性。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：在一组形状相似的对象中，找出与\"模板\"对象形状完全匹配的那些，并将它们连接到模板对象上。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格中有一个用 Red 颜色绘制的\"模板\"对象（一个小型 4-连通形状，3-5 像素），位于网格中央。\n  - 网格中散布若干个相同大小的 4-连通对象，部分对象的归一化形状（允许旋转和翻转）与模板匹配，部分不匹配。匹配对象使用 Blue 颜色，不匹配对象使用 Green 颜色。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 保留 Red 模板对象和所有 Blue 对象不变。\n  - 将所有 Green 对象擦除为背景色。\n  - 对每个 Blue 对象，从该对象到 Red 模板之间画一条 Yellow 的直线连接（水平或垂直，取较短路径），连接两者最近的边界像素。\n\n- `Key insight`：颜色已经编码了匹配结果（Blue = 匹配，Green = 不匹配），但解题者仍需归纳出这一编码规则并发现连接线的绘制逻辑。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将网格中每个连通区域的边界像素保留，内部像素替换为该区域所包含的孔洞数量对应的颜色。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格中有若干个 4-连通单色前景对象，每个对象为不同颜色且形状各异。\n  - 部分对象内部包含背景色孔洞（4-连通的被完全包围的背景区域），孔洞数量从 0 到 3 不等。\n  - 网格边缘有一个简单的颜色图例：四个纵向排列的色块，从上到下分别代表孔洞数量 0、1、2、3 对应的填充颜色。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个前景对象，保留其边界像素（至少有一个 4-邻居为背景或其他颜色的像素）的原色不变。\n  - 计算该对象内部的 4-连通背景孔洞数量 H。\n  - 从图例中查找 H 对应的颜色，将该对象所有非边界像素（内部像素）替换为该颜色。\n  - 孔洞本身保持为背景色。\n\n- `Key insight`：拓扑特征（孔洞数量）作为查找键索引颜色图例，这需要解题者同时理解\"孔洞计数\"和\"图例映射\"两层逻辑。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n===== prompt =====\n你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"973e499e\" lines=\"7-22\">\n<description>\nExpand each input pixel into a miniature same-color mask of the whole grid.\n\nInput structure\n- The input is a non-empty two-dimensional grid of foreground colors.\n- Black is reserved for the empty/background pixels introduced in the expanded output.\n- The output has one input-shaped block for each input pixel.\n\nRule\n- For every input pixel with color c, replace that pixel by a block the same shape as the input.\n- Inside the block, write c exactly where the original input also has color c.\n- Write black everywhere else in the block.\n\nKey insight\nEach pixel selects the global mask of its own color; the result is the blockwise self-mask of the grid.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"f8cc533f\" lines=\"10-25\">\n<description>\nComplete every colored sprite by applying the union of all aligned partial sprite masks.\n\nInput structure:\n- The dominant color is the background.\n- Each non-background color appears as a separated partial copy of one common sprite mask.\n- The copies share a top-left-aligned sprite window; some copies may be missing lower or right edge pixels.\n\nRule:\n- Crop each same-color mask to its bounding box.\n- Pad the crops to the maximum observed height and width, aligned at the top-left, and OR them into one complete template.\n- Fill that template at every sprite location using the sprite's own color.\n\nKey insight:\n- No single input sprite is complete, but their missing cells are complementary, so the aligned union reveals the full mask.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"89565ca0\" lines=\"120-136\">\n<description>\nConvert each colored partitioned frame into a horizontal bar whose length is its number of enclosed regions.\n\nInput structure:\n- Black background with several axis-aligned colored line drawings.\n- The line drawings are damaged by scattered pixels of one non-background noise color and by overlaps with other drawings.\n- Each real drawing is a rectangular partitioned frame enclosing one or more background regions.\n\nRule:\n- For each non-background color, reconstruct its horizontal and vertical wall segments from dense row/column evidence.\n- Count the 4-connected background regions fully enclosed by those reconstructed walls.\n- The color with no enclosed region is the noise/pad color.\n- Sort drawing colors by enclosed-region count; equal counts are ordered by which reconstructed frame covers the other.\n\nKey insight:\n- The scattered color is not an object; it only pads the histogram, while each true object's room count is stable after rectilinear wall reconstruction.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2b9ef948\" lines=\"51-65\">\n<description>\nMove the yellow 3x3 frame by the displacement encoded by the gray path, then draw its diagonal yellow corner rays.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is black.\n- One 3x3 yellow frame has a non-yellow control-color center.\n- A second control-color pixel is connected through gray path pixels to a lone yellow endpoint.\n\nRule:\n- Use the vector from the second control-color pixel to the lone yellow endpoint as the frame's translation.\n- Fill the whole output with the control color.\n- Draw the translated yellow frame and extend yellow diagonal rays outward from its four corners to the grid edge.\n\nKey insight: The gray path's turns are irrelevant; its two colored endpoints encode the net displacement to apply to the frame.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"6e4f6532\" lines=\"26-41\">\n<description>\nDock train sprites onto station groups by matching coupler count, then orient via divider-color markers.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg; colored stripes (edge + internal) partition grid into rectangular regions.\n- Color 8 forms train bodies; color 9 marks both isolated stations and train-attached couplers.\n- Stripe-colored pixels on trains are orientation markers.\n\nRule:\n- Stations = 8-connected 9-clusters not adjacent to any 8. Trains = components containing 8.\n- Match train to station group where |couplers| == |station size|.\n- Rotate/flip train so marker pixels face the same-color boundary stripe of the target region.\n- Translate so couplers align exactly onto station cells; erase original position.\n\nKey insight: Coupler count selects the docking target; marker color encodes which boundary stripe to face, fixing the unique orientation.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"db7260a4\" lines=\"37-56\">\n<description>\nDrop the singleton marker into the matching red U-shaped container, or make a bottom-row puddle if no closed container is hit.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a dominant background, one singleton marker pixel on the top row,\n  and one other foreground color forming vertical bars and bottom segments.\n- A closed container is a U shape: two vertical side bars with a continuous\n  bottom segment between them and an empty rectangular interior above the bottom.\n\nRule\n- Remove the top marker from its original cell.\n- If exactly one closed U-shaped container has the marker column within its\n  horizontal footprint, fill that container's empty interior with the marker color.\n- If no closed container is under the marker column, fill the whole bottom row\n  with the marker color.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker does not identify a color by value; it identifies a vertical drop\n  column, and only a structurally closed U shape can catch and contain the fill.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2faf500b\" lines=\"30-44\">\n<description>\nRemove each fracture marker line and push the surrounding object pixels one cell away from it.\n\nInput structure\n- A background grid with 8-connected foreground objects made from a body color and a rarer marker color.\n- Each object has a non-square bbox; the marker pixels form one complete fracture line across the shorter bbox axis.\n\nRule\n- Erase all marker pixels.\n- For a wide object, each row has one marker; body pixels left of it shift one cell left and body pixels right of it shift one cell right.\n- For a tall object, each column has one marker; body pixels above it shift one cell up and body pixels below it shift one cell down.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker line is a crack through the object, so the two sides separate by one pixel perpendicular to the crack.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"f18ec8cc\" lines=\"71-86\">\n<description>\nReorder the vertical color-major blocks while preserving every block's internal pixels.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid is divided into vertical blocks, each with a unique dominant color.\nSmall marker pixels from other block colors may appear inside the blocks.\n\nRule\nIf adjacent shared-color marker rows read exactly as the current block order\nfrom right to left, reverse the blocks. Otherwise move the leftmost block to\nthe far right and shift the remaining blocks left.\n\nKey insight\nThe transformation acts on whole vertical blocks, so marker pixels move with\ntheir source block instead of being recolored or independently rearranged.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"981add89\" lines=\"10-29\">\n<description>\nExtend each top-row control pixel downward as a vertical toggle ray in its own color.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Non-background pixels on the top row are control pixels, each identifying\n  one column and one ray color.\n- Foreground regions below may intersect these control columns.\n\nRule:\n- For every top-row control pixel, process the cells below it in the same\n  column down to the bottom edge.\n- A cell that already has the control color is erased to the background.\n- Every other cell on that downward ray is painted with the control color.\n- The top-row control pixels themselves remain unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\nThe top row is a set of vertical ray launchers; each ray toggles only cells\nmatching its own color and overwrites all other colors along that column.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"337b420f\" lines=\"41-55\">\n<description>\nKeep the larger sprite from each separated panel and overlay those sprites into one 5x5 canvas.\n\nInput structure:\n- The input is a 5x17 grid: three 5x5 panels separated by one-cell black columns.\n- Each panel has the same background color and exactly one foreground color split into two 4-connected components.\n\nRule:\n- In each panel, discard the smaller foreground component and keep the unique largest component as the sprite.\n- Process panels left to right, placing each sprite at its panel coordinates on a 5x5 background canvas.\n- If a sprite would cover an already placed sprite, slide it by the unique nearest in-bounds offset that avoids overlap.\n\nKey insight:\n- The extra same-colored component in each panel is a distractor; the final answer is the non-overlapping overlay of the three largest components.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"878187ab\" lines=\"10-24\">\n<description>\nReplace the scattered foreground markers with a bottom-left count rectangle whose two corner diagonals encode the marker counts.\n\nInput structure\n- A background grid with exactly two foreground colors used as scattered marker pixels.\n- The two foreground colors have distinct pixel counts.\n\nRule\n- Ignore marker positions and use only the two foreground counts.\n- Make a 16-by-16 background canvas, fill a bottom-left red rectangle whose height is the smaller count and width is the larger count.\n- Paint yellow pixels along the two rising 45-degree diagonals from the rectangle's bottom-left and bottom-right corners.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker colors and positions vary between examples; their counts alone determine the output rectangle dimensions.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"50c07299\" lines=\"8-21\">\n<description>\nMove the diagonal foreground segment to the next longer run along the same up-right diagonal.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has one background color and one foreground color. The foreground pixels form a\ncontiguous one-pixel-wide segment on a single anti-diagonal.\n\nRule\nErase the current segment. If its columns are c0..c1 and its length is L, draw the same\ncolor on columns c1+1..c1+L+1 along the same anti-diagonal.\n\nKey insight\nThe segment advances past its current upper-right end by one whole segment position, and\nthe next segment is one pixel longer than the current one.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"13\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"2ba387bc\" lines=\"6-21\">\n<description>\nSort scattered 4×4 squares into two columns by type: frames left, solids right.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Multiple 4×4 objects on bg.\n- Frames: colored 1px border, bg-filled 2×2 interior.\n- Solids: entirely filled with one non-bg color.\n\nRule:\n- Classify each 4×4 object as frame or solid by its interior.\n- Sort each group top-to-bottom by input row.\n- Stack frames in left column (cols 0–3), solids in right (cols 4–7).\n- Output is 8 wide; height = 4 × max(#frames, #solids), bg-padded.\n\nKey insight: Frame vs solid is determined solely by whether the 2×2 interior matches bg.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport ast\nfiles = [\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/581f7754.py',\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dbff022c.py',\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/88e364bc.py',\n]\nfor fp in files:\n    text = Path(fp).read_text()\n    lines = text.splitlines()\n    tree = ast.parse(text)\n    print(f'===== {fp} =====')\n    wanted = set()\n    for node in tree.body:\n        if isinstance(node, ast.Assign):\n            for t in node.targets:\n                if getattr(t, 'id', None) in {'_GEN_RETRY_LIMIT','_MAX_RETRIES','GEN_RETRIES'}:\n                    wanted.add((node.lineno,node.end_lineno))\n        if isinstance(node, ast.FunctionDef) and node.name in {'_gen_attempt','generate_input'}:\n            wanted.add((node.lineno,node.end_lineno))\n    for start,end in sorted(wanted):\n        print(f'--- lines {start}-{end} ---')\n        for i in range(start-1, min(end, start+170)-1):\n            print(f'{i+1:4}: {lines[i]}')\n        if end-start > 170:\n            print('...')\n    print()\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport ast\nfiles = [\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/581f7754.py',\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dbff022c.py',\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/88e364bc.py',\n]\nfor fp in files:\n    text = Path(fp).read_text()\n    lines = text.splitlines()\n    tree = ast.parse(text)\n    print(f'===== {fp} =====')\n    wanted = set()\n    for node in tree.body:\n        if isinstance(node, ast.Assign):\n            for t in node.targets:\n                if getattr(t, 'id', None) in {'_GEN_RETRY_LIMIT','_MAX_RETRIES','GEN_RETRIES'}:\n                    wanted.add((node.lineno,node.end_lineno))\n        if isinstance(node, ast.FunctionDef) and node.name in {'_gen_attempt','generate_input'}:\n            wanted.add((node.lineno,node.end_lineno))\n    for start,end in sorted(wanted):\n        print(f'--- lines {start}-{end} ---')\n        for i in range(start-1, min(end, start+170)-1):\n            print(f'{i+1:4}: {lines[i]}')\n        if end-start > 170:\n            print('...')\n    print()\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"===== /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/581f7754.py =====\n--- lines 155-155 ---\n--- lines 487-505 ---\n 487: def _gen_attempt():\n 488:     bg, out, inp = _new_canvas_pair()\n 489:     placed = _place_anchors(out, inp, bg)\n 490:     if placed is None:\n 491:         return None\n 492:     anchor_colors, anchors = placed\n 493: \n 494:     marker_colors = _marker_color_sequence(anchor_colors)\n 495:     sprites = _place_aligned_sprites(out, anchors, marker_colors, bg)\n 496:     if sprites is None:\n 497:         return None\n 498: \n 499:     if not _scatter_sprites(inp, sprites, bg):\n 500:         return None\n 501: \n 502:     _add_distractors(out, inp, anchors, bg)\n 503:     if not _generated_grid_is_valid(inp, out, bg):\n 504:         return None\n--- lines 582-587 ---\n 582: def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n 583:     for _ in range(_GEN_RETRY_LIMIT):\n 584:         grid = _gen_attempt()\n 585:         if grid is not None:\n 586:             return grid\n\n===== /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dbff022c.py =====\n--- lines 327-327 ---\n--- lines 449-541 ---\n 449: def _gen_attempt():\n 450:     rng = random.Random()\n 451:     bg = 0\n 452: \n 453:     # Grid size and palette side\n 454:     H = rng.randint(_GRID_H_MIN, _GRID_H_MAX)\n 455:     W = rng.randint(_GRID_W_MIN, _GRID_W_MAX)\n 456:     side = rng.choice(['top', 'bottom', 'left', 'right'])\n 457:     if H <= _SMALL_H_THRESHOLD and side in ('top', 'bottom') and rng.random() < _SMALL_H_PALETTE_FLIP:\n 458:         side = rng.choice(['left', 'right'])\n 459: \n 460:     max_N = H if side in ('left', 'right') else W\n 461:     N = rng.randint(_PALETTE_N_MIN, min(_PALETTE_N_MAX, max_N))\n 462: \n 463:     # Sprite dimension bounds\n 464:     max_sh = min(_SPRITE_H_MAX, H)\n 465:     max_sw = min(_SPRITE_W_MAX, W)\n 466:     if H <= _TINY_H_THRESHOLD:\n 467:         max_sh = 3\n 468: \n 469:     # Sprite counts\n 470:     num_filled = rng.randint(1, min(_FILLED_SPRITE_MAX, N))\n 471:     total_sprites = num_filled + 1\n 472: \n 473:     # Generate sprite shapes\n 474:     shapes = []\n 475:     for _ in range(total_sprites):\n 476:         sh = rng.randint(3, max_sh)\n 477:         sw = rng.randint(3, max_sw)\n 478:         if sh + sw > _SPRITE_DIM_SUM_CAP:\n 479:             sw = max(3, _SPRITE_DIM_SUM_CAP - sh)\n 480:         if sh == 3 and sw == 3 and rng.random() < _P_DIAMOND:\n 481:             mask = _make_diamond()\n 482:         else:\n 483:             mask = _make_hollow_sprite(sh, sw, rng)\n 484:         if mask is None:\n 485:             return None\n 486:         shapes.append(mask)\n 487: \n 488:     # Colors and palette\n 489:     border_keys, fill_values, distractor_color, mapping, filled_keys = \\\n 490:         _choose_colors(rng, N, num_filled)\n 491:     pal = _build_palette(side, border_keys, fill_values)\n 492: \n 493:     grid = np.full((H, W), bg, dtype=int)\n 494:     occ = np.zeros((H, W), dtype=bool)\n 495:     _place_palette(grid, occ, pal, side, rng)\n 496: \n 497:     # Assign colors to sprites: filled sprites use palette keys, last one is distractor\n 498:     infos = []\n 499:     for i, mask in enumerate(shapes):\n 500:         if i < num_filled:\n 501:             c, f = filled_keys[i], mapping[filled_keys[i]]\n 502:         else:\n 503:             c, f = distractor_color, None\n 504:         infos.append((mask, c, f))\n 505: \n 506:     # Place sprites\n 507:     placed = []\n 508:     for mask, color, fill in infos:\n 509:         holes = _get_enclosed_holes(mask)\n 510:         positions = _find_valid_positions(H, W, occ, mask, holes)\n 511:         if not positions:\n 512:             return None\n 513:         r0, c0 = rng.choice(positions)\n 514:         _paint_sprite(grid, r0, c0, mask, color, fill, holes)\n 515:         placed.append((r0, c0, mask, fill))\n 516:         sh, sw = mask.shape\n 517:         occ[max(0, r0 - 1):min(H, r0 + sh + 1),\n 518:             max(0, c0 - 1):min(W, c0 + sw + 1)] = True\n 519: \n 520:     # Derive input from output by clearing filled holes\n 521:     output = grid.copy()\n 522:     inp = grid.copy()\n 523:     for r0, c0, mask, fill in placed:\n 524:         if fill is not None:\n 525:             for hpts in _get_enclosed_holes(mask):\n 526:                 for hr, hc in hpts:\n 527:                     inp[r0 + hr, c0 + hc] = bg\n 528: \n 529:     # Validate bg is dominant on border\n 530:     border = np.concatenate([inp[0], inp[-1], inp[1:-1, 0], inp[1:-1, -1]])\n 531:     vals, cnts = np.unique(border, return_counts=True)\n 532:     if int(vals[cnts.argmax()]) != bg:\n 533:         return None\n 534: \n 535:     # Oracle check\n 536:     try:\n 537:         if np.array_equal(main(inp), output):\n 538:             return inp\n 539:     except Exception:\n 540:         pass\n--- lines 544-549 ---\n 544: def generate_input():\n 545:     for _ in range(_MAX_RETRIES):\n 546:         r = _gen_attempt()\n 547:         if r is not None:\n 548:             return r\n\n===== /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/88e364bc.py =====\n--- lines 199-199 ---\n--- lines 579-601 ---\n 579: def _gen_attempt(rng: random.Random) -> np.ndarray | None:\n 580:     h, w = GRID_H, GRID_W\n 581:     grid = np.zeros((h, w), dtype=int)\n 582: \n 583:     legend_occupied, legends = _place_legends(rng, grid)\n 584:     regions = _grow_regions(rng, legends, legend_occupied)\n 585:     if regions is None:\n 586:         return None\n 587: \n 588:     # Paint walls.\n 589:     for reg in regions:\n 590:         for r, c in reg['walls']:\n 591:             grid[r, c] = reg['color']\n 592: \n 593:     if not _validate_topology(grid, regions):\n 594:         return None\n 595: \n 596:     input_grid = grid.copy()\n 597:     if not _place_yellows(rng, regions, input_grid):\n 598:         return None\n 599:     if not _oracle_check(input_grid, regions):\n 600:         return None\n--- lines 604-613 ---\n 604: def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n 605:     rng = random.Random()\n 606:     for _ in range(GEN_RETRIES):\n 607:         try:\n 608:             g = _gen_attempt(rng)\n 609:         except Exception:\n 610:             continue\n 611:         if g is not None:\n 612:             return g\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
